AWebWEBP plugin
===============

The AWebWEBP plugin for AWeb (version 3.6 or higher) allows you
to view WebP (Web Picture) images directly inside the browser.
WebP is Google's modern image format used widely on the web; it
provides better compression than JPEG and PNG and supports
lossless mode and full alpha transparency.

Features include:

 * Decodes both lossy (VP8) and lossless (VP8L) WebP bitstreams
 * Full alpha-channel transparency through the standard AWeb
   planar mask path
 * Optional progressive display of loading images
 * Support for image scaling
 * Native Picasso96 deep-bitmap rendering on RTG screens
 * Fall-back to classic 8-bit planar bitmaps on AGA/ECS screens
   with hashed ObtainBestPen for fast colour mapping

The AWeb WebP plugin is copyright (c) 2026 amigazen project.
It uses Google's libwebp library version 0.2.0 distributed under a
BSD-style licence; see webplib/README.txt for details.
